WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
A hormone reaches a liver cell.

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.490
It binds to the outside,
and it never goes in.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.640
Yet inside, glycogen starts breaking down,

4
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.140
and glucose pours out of the cell.

5
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.750
A few hormone molecules on the outside.

6
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.900
Thousands of sugar molecules freed inside.

7
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.650
So how does such a small
signal grow so large?

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.980
In this mission, you'll meet receptors
that cross the membrane seven times,

9
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.220
and the G proteins they switch on.

10
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.820
Then you'll follow the
message inside the liver cell,

11
00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.780
and meet a second messenger.

12
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.560
Your mission: explain how a few hormone
molecules can free thousands of sugar

13
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.490
molecules.
